class.description:
A transport creates peers of one [MultiplayerPeer] class, lists servers, and checks a server without joining it. Register it with [method NetwConnectHandle.register_transport]. For WebRTC, see [NetwWebRTCSignaler].
[codeblock]
class_name RelayTransport
extends NetwTransport

func _peer_class() -> StringName:
    return &"RelayMultiplayerPeer"

func _host_settings() -> Dictionary:
    return {region = "eu"}

func _make_peer(
        ticket: RID, mode: NetwMultiplayer.TransportMode,
        address: String, settings: Dictionary) -> void:
    report(ticket, &"handshake", "Reaching the relay...", 0.5)
    var peer := RelayMultiplayerPeer.new()
    var err: Error = await peer.connect_async(address, settings.region)
    if err != OK:
        fail(ticket, ERR_CANT_CONNECT, "relay rejected")
        return
    _room = peer.room
    deliver(ticket, peer)

func _join_address() -> String:
    return _room

# somewhere in the game
func _ready() -> void:
    Netw.connection(self).register_transport(RelayTransport)
[/codeblock]
[method _make_peer] and [method _probe] may [code]await[/code]. They report the result by calling [method deliver], [method deliver_probe] or [method fail] once, with the [param ticket] they received. Keep [param ticket] in a local variable, not a member, since another request may start while one awaits. With no report, the request fails after [method _timeout_hint] seconds.
Methods starting with an underscore are overridden. Each has a public method that calls it, and a [code]_default[/code] method with the default behavior.

method.description:
Return the fields a join form asks for, with their default values. They are passed to [method _make_peer] in [constant NetwMultiplayer.TRANSPORT_MODE_CLIENT].
[codeblock]
func _client_settings() -> Dictionary:
    return {region = "eu"}

func _host_settings() -> Dictionary:
    var settings := _client_settings()
    settings.max_players = 32
    return settings
[/codeblock]

Reports the servers [method _browse] found, one per address. [param names] and [param infos] are matched to [param addresses] by index, and can be shorter.
[codeblock]
func _browse() -> void:
    var lobbies := await _sdk.search()
    var addresses := PackedStringArray()
    var names := PackedStringArray()
    var infos: Array[NetwServerInfo] = []
    for lobby in lobbies:
        addresses.append(lobby.id)
        names.append(lobby.name)
        infos.append(_info_of(lobby))
    publish_targets(addresses, names, infos)
[/codeblock]
